  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Critical Edition",
    "overview": "The AI's text is one witness. Every screen is set like a scholarly edition: a white page carrying the reading text in Garamond, the other models' readings and the researcher's corrections set beneath it as an apparatus criticus, each witness named by a red siglum. The shell around the page is bookcloth: a deep blue rail and masthead, the binding the edition sits in. Controls are quiet, in a humanist sans, so the text keeps the authority. The source (a scan or a recording) rests on a grey desk beside the page, an object on a table rather than a panel in an app.\n\nDensity is that of a working edition, not a dashboard: generous measure for reading text, compact controls, hairline rules for structure. Sections open with a black rule, the way an edition opens its apparatus, and are never boxed. The world refuses two things by name: the AI-product arrangement of glowing cards and chat bubbles, and the parchment costume the name \"Scriptorium\" invites. There is no paper texture, no aged tint, no faux manuscript ornament.\n\nThe same world holds from a 640px window snapped beside another to a 2560px monitor, and in light and dark themes that follow Windows by default.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White page ground, bookcloth blue (#1d2b4f) shell, black text.",
      "Rubric red reserved for sigla, marginal line numbers and the researcher's corrections.",
      "Pale blue tint for selection and highlighted lemmata.",
      "EB Garamond for everything read; Source Sans 3 for everything operated.",
      "Sections divided by rules, never cards; shadows only on objects lifted off the desk and on overlays.",
      "Lucide line icons at a 1.5px stroke, always after or beside words."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Rubric Rule",
        "body": "Rubric red marks only sigla, marginal line numbers and the researcher's corrections. If something red is neither a witness's name, a line reference nor a correction, it is wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bookcloth Rule",
        "body": "Blue owns the binding (rail, mastheads) and the actions. It is not a decorative fill for sections on the page.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Desk Rule",
        "body": "Desk grey sits only behind a source. The edition page and every form sit on white.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Faces Rule",
        "body": "Garamond carries reading text, titles, the wordmark, small-caps running heads and sigla. Source Sans 3 carries every control. A button, field, tab or label in Garamond is a defect; a document text in the sans is a defect.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Quarantine Rule",
        "body": "Monospace appears only in the prompt editor, because prompt text is written like code. Nowhere else.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Shadowed Cards Rule",
        "body": "Sections never get a shadow, a fill or a box. If a section needs separating, it gets the section rule.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** open every section with the 1px section rule and nothing else around it.",
      "**Do** keep rubric red (#b3261e / #ec8478) for sigla, marginal line numbers and corrections only.",
      "**Do** use lemma tint (#dce3f2) for selection, marked lemmata and the playing segment.",
      "**Do** set anything read (documents, titles, running heads, sigla) in EB Garamond and every control in Source Sans 3.",
      "**Do** put sources (scans, players) on the desk grey, with the flyout shadow, and keep the edition on white.",
      "**Do** keep the masthead and the rail's wordmark block at the same 6.5rem so their rules meet.",
      "**Do** put words before icons; use Lucide icons through `Icon.svelte`.",
      "**Do** design for 640px to 2560px, with the shell collapsing at 820px, review stacking at 960px and reading text rising at 1680px."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** box sections in cards, fill them, or give them shadows.",
      "**Don't** add parchment, paper texture, aged tints or manuscript ornament.",
      "**Don't** use glowing cards, gradients or chat-bubble styling.",
      "**Don't** use red for decoration, emphasis or status; errors use danger red as text, not rubric.",
      "**Don't** use monospace outside the prompt editor.",
      "**Don't** use glyph characters (arrows, crosses, triangles) as icons.",
      "**Don't** hard-code visible text; every string comes from the translation files."
